{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02413",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 5.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Hmm, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.77,
      "end_seconds": 12.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.72,
      "end_seconds": 22.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this. Doctor, it's yellow crusts. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.45,
      "end_seconds": 29.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.82,
      "end_seconds": 37.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed. I take a moisturiser, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.63,
      "end_seconds": 41.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.45,
      "end_seconds": 51.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "I've had it for six months. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.15,
      "end_seconds": 59.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.55,
      "end_seconds": 66.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Well, when it starts I tend to get being irritable as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.89,
      "end_seconds": 73.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 73.94,
      "end_seconds": 81.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "I mean, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.16,
      "end_seconds": 84.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.95,
      "end_seconds": 91.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.2,
      "end_seconds": 103.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Alright, any high fever or drowsiness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.13,
      "end_seconds": 117.5,
      "duration_seconds": 13.37,
      "text": "No, no high fever, no drowsiness. I did have itchy red patches that have gone crusty at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.21,
      "end_seconds": 122.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Have you had any eating poorly or blisters?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.23,
      "end_seconds": 130.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.89,
      "end_seconds": 135.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.77,
      "end_seconds": 141.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.66,
      "end_seconds": 157.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.43,
      "end_seconds": 166.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Oh, yes, I had my appendix taken out, when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.61,
      "end_seconds": 171.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.56,
      "end_seconds": 182.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "I have eczema, for nearly five years. Right, uh, I've had arthritis in my knees for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.02,
      "end_seconds": 193.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Right, so arthritis in your knees is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.05,
      "end_seconds": 198.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.8,
      "end_seconds": 203.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.26,
      "end_seconds": 208.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.37,
      "end_seconds": 211.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.72,
      "end_seconds": 217.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.07,
      "end_seconds": 223.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.85,
      "end_seconds": 231.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.1,
      "end_seconds": 261.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 66, BP is 108 over 71, respiratory rate 18. And temperature is 36.7 degrees, saturation 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.74,
      "end_seconds": 264.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.85,
      "end_seconds": 268.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.97,
      "end_seconds": 273.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.11,
      "end_seconds": 277.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.56,
      "end_seconds": 291.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "The eczema patches on the arms have yellow crusts and weeping areas."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.71,
      "end_seconds": 318.14,
      "duration_seconds": 21.43,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. So, based on the history and the examination, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at eczema with a bacterial skin infection or herpes simplex eczema. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had yellow crusts for six months, and no blisters or high fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.8,
      "end_seconds": 319.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.34,
      "end_seconds": 323.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "We should do a skin swab for infected eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 325.74,
      "end_seconds": 329.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I can book that for Friday at 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.94,
      "end_seconds": 352.31,
      "duration_seconds": 22.37,
      "text": "I'd like you to take flucloxacillin, 250 milligrams, four times a day, seven days. That should help with infected eczema. Keep the nails short and keep using the moisturiser. I'll want another look in one week. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.92,
      "end_seconds": 361.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Let me think, um, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}